# ORCLPEDE: the centipede, which is four stats pretending to be one animal (M16.5).
#
# Both trains carry P1 0 and P2 0, and that is what makes a centipede
# comparable at all. ElementCentipedeHeadTick opens with three gates:
#
#   (X = playerX) and (Random(10) < P1)      -> turn onto the player's column
#   (Y = playerY) and (Random(10) < P1)      -> turn onto the player's row
#   ((Random(10) * 4) < P2) or step is zero  -> pick a random direction
#
# P1 0 makes `Random(10) < 0` unsatisfiable and P2 0 does the same for the
# deviance gate, so a head with an authored step simply keeps it — from anywhere
# on the board, with no alignment requirement at all. That is unlike every other
# creature in this sweep, and it is why the player can walk away from these
# trains without stranding them in a random draw.
#
# The blocked-path logic underneath is random too — it turns onto a perpendicular
# chosen by `((Random(2) * 2) - 1)` — and it is forced the same way M16.4 forced
# the spinning gun: both corridors are exactly one square wide, so BOTH
# perpendiculars are walls whichever way the draw lands, and the code falls
# through to the deterministic tail: reverse onto `-ix, -iy`, and if that is
# blocked too (it is — the train's own next segment is there), zero the step.
# A zeroed step is what makes a centipede turn around: the head becomes a
# segment, the leader/follower chain is walked and flipped end to end, and the
# TAIL becomes the head. Train B does that against the dead end at 5,9 and again
# at 25,9, so the reversal is caught at both ends of its corridor.
#
# Nothing is authored as a linked train: every segment starts with Leader and
# Follower -1, exactly as the ZZT editor leaves them, and the head adopts them on
# its first move — the `repeat ... until statId = -1` loop that looks one square
# behind, then to either side, for an unclaimed segment. The trains would fall
# apart on the first tick if that loop were wrong.
#
# Train A marches down the player's own corridor and bites four times, once per
# stat. ElementCentipedeHeadTick promotes its own follower to head BEFORE
# attacking, so each bite costs the player 10 health and the train one stat, and
# the last stat in the train has no follower left to promote: 100 -> 60.
#
# Train B is then walked into from the side, through the one gap at 12,10.
# ElementDamagingTouch on a SEGMENT costs the player 10 health and removes that
# segment, cutting the train in half. The rear half's leader is gone, so
# ElementCentipedeSegmentTick — whose whole body is a countdown from Leader -1 —
# turns it into a head two ticks later and it marches off on its own. That is
# the only path through that proc, and the cut is the only way to reach it.
#
# There is no shooting in this world, and the reason is worth recording: a bullet
# fired down a one-square-wide corridor never kills a head. The head is blocked
# by the oncoming bullet, and a blocked head in a one-wide corridor reverses, so
# the bullet lands on the tail-turned-front instead. Bullets against creatures
# are pinned in fire.scn, where the target is a bear standing in the open.
world ORCLPEDE
seed 0
phase
boot 240
capture title
play
# Pede Hub: unpause and cross the east border opening at 60,13.
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture arrive
# Both trains march west; train B reaches its dead end first and flips.
settle 48
capture linked
settle 4
capture reversed-west
# Train A arrives at the player and bites once per stat.
settle 16
capture first-bite
settle 14
capture bites-done
# Train B turns around again at the far end of its corridor.
settle 34
capture reversed-east
# Up through the gap at 4,12 into the hall, then east to train B's own gap.
move right
move right
move right
move up
move up
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
move right
capture at-gap
move up
capture in-gap
# Wait in the gap for the train to come back past it, so what the player walks
# into is a SEGMENT and not the head or bare floor.
settle 48
capture train-passing
move up
capture segment-touched
settle 6
capture segment-promoted
settle 12
capture train-cut
